                <pb facs="0913" n="828" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg828"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">860j.01/39a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Davis</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-08-11T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 11,
                                1919, 5 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>5795. My 5792, August 9, 1919, 7 p.m.</p>
                <p>In view of gravity of situation and necessity of immediate action you are
                    instructed to urge British Government with all earnestness not to withdraw
                    troops from Batum for time being.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
